  "text": "The coordinates of the centers and radii of circles $C_1$ and $C_2$ are as follows:\n\n$C_1: (1, 2)$, radius $r_1 = \\sqrt{(0^2-1^2)+(0^2-2^2)} = \\sqrt{5}$\n\n$C_2: (-1, 3)$, radius $r_2 = \\sqrt{(-2^2-(\\sqrt{5})^2)}$.\n\nThe direction vector of the line passing through the centers is $(0-1, 0-2) = (-1,-2)$. This direction vector makes an angle $\\theta$ with the x-axis, where $\\tan\\theta = -2/1$. Therefore, the equation of the line passing through $C_1$ and $C_2$ is $y-2 = (\\tan\\theta)(x-1)$.\n\nTo find the equation of the tangent line, we need to find the values of $x$ and $y$ such that the distance from the original center to the point of tangency is equal to the radius of the circle. This can be done by solving the following system of equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2 \\\\\n(x^2+y^2-2x-4y+1=0) \\\\\n(y-2) = (\\tan\\theta)(x-1) \\\\\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ is the center of the circle and $r$ is its radius. In this case, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n(x-1)^2+(y-2)^2=5 \\\\\n(x^2+y^2+2x-6y+2=0) \\\\\n(y-2) = (\\tan\\theta)(x-1) \\\\\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSolving the first equation for $y$ and substituting into the second equation, we get:\n\n\\[\nx^2-5+x-2y=0 \\\\\n(x^2+y^2+2x-6y+2=0) \\\\\n\\times 2 \\\\\n2x^2+2y^2+4x-12y+4=0 \\\\\n(x^2+y^2-2x-4y+1=0) \\\\\n\\times 1 \\\\\nx^2+y^2-2x-4y+1=0 \\\\\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nThen we compare these two equations to get:\n\n\\[\nx^2+2x^2-2x-6x-4y+4y-x+y=0 \\\\\nx^2+y^2=0 \\\\\n\\]\n\nWhich means that the point of tangency is on the line that passes through the centers. Thus, the desired line is the line passing through the centers of the circles $C_1$ and $C_2$. Therefore, the equation of the tangent line is:\n\n$$y-2 = (\\tan\\theta)(x-1)$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\tan\\theta$, we can use the direction vector of the line passing through the centers, which is $(1,2)$. Thus, we have:\n\n$$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{2}{1} = 2$$\n\nTherefore, the desired line is:\n\n$$y-2 = 2(x-1)$$\n\n$$y = 2x$$\n\nPutting this into our last form, we get:\n\n$$\\boxed{y = 2x}$$",
